# Prettier formats content/ (tables, spacing) — see .prettierrc.json.
#
# It must NOT touch the raw payload of Hugo shortcodes that carry code or math,
# because its markdown parser reads that payload as prose and rewrites it:
#   * {{< chart >}} holds Chart.js JavaScript. `(_, i)` became `(\_, i)` and
#     `i * 10` became `i _ 10`, since both look like markdown emphasis.
#   * {{< katex >}} holds LaTeX with `_` subscripts and `*`, at the same risk.
# Both also lose their indentation, because the payload is one long paragraph.
#
# Those blocks are therefore fenced off in the markdown itself with a
# `<!-- prettier-ignore -->` comment on the line directly above the opening
# shortcode. Add that comment whenever you add a new chart or katex block.
